WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.817
Read the case as a set of cooperating
responsibilities and data rules.

00:00:04.817 --> 00:00:09.978
Public pages, contributions and volunteer actions
exercise different paths.

00:00:09.978 --> 00:00:16.447
Resource-oriented HTTP design can clarify an
interface, but it does not supply access control.

00:00:16.447 --> 00:00:22.916
Preserve schema integrity and identify external
dependencies before deciding which part of the

00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:25.531
historical architecture should change.

00:00:25.531 --> 00:00:30.709
Object storage and a CDN separate media delivery
from application processing.

00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:37.165
Thumbnails reduce payload for different displays,
while caching can reduce repeated origin work.

00:00:37.165 --> 00:00:39.586
Random names are not access control.

00:00:39.586 --> 00:00:46.311
The cost charts are historical context from 2020, so
use them to understand tradeoffs rather than as

00:00:46.311 --> 00:00:49.808
current infrastructure prices or guaranteed savings.
